<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--Over-map chrome.

        Panels that float on the map canvas (scalebar, coordinate readout, legend card, sketch
        bar, the extent handles) must stay legible against arbitrary basemap imagery — satellite,
        street, dark, or a blank white raster. They therefore do NOT follow the app theme, and
        deliberately do not appear in Status.Light/Dark.xaml.

        This dictionary exists so that intent is written down. Before it, those surfaces were
        raw Background="White" and Stroke="White" literals scattered across eight files, which
        read as theme bugs and invited exactly the wrong fix.

        Rule of thumb: if removing the map behind the element would make a theme brush correct,
        it is chrome and belongs on MahApps.Brushes.*; if the element has to survive whatever
        imagery is underneath it, it belongs here.-->

    <!--backing plate for a readout or a small floating panel-->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="IRI.Maptor.Brushes.OnMap.Surface" Color="#F2FFFFFF"/>

    <!--text and glyphs sitting on OnMap.Surface-->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="IRI.Maptor.Brushes.OnMap.Text" Color="#FF1A1A1A"/>

    <!--hairline around an OnMap.Surface-->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="IRI.Maptor.Brushes.OnMap.Border" Color="#33000000"/>

    <!--outline that keeps a marker, handle or label readable directly on imagery,
        with no backing plate-->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="IRI.Maptor.Brushes.OnMap.Halo" Color="#FFFFFFFF"/>

    <!--fill of a draggable handle on the map (extent corners, vertex grips)-->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="IRI.Maptor.Brushes.OnMap.HandleFill" Color="#FFFFFFFF"/>

    <!--Ink for text or glyphs sitting directly ON an accent fill.

        This has to be fixed rather than themed, and the reason is not obvious: the MahApps accent
        is the SAME colour in the light and dark themes, and in the Amber theme this app ships it
        is a light colour in both. So neither ThemeForeground (white in dark) nor IdealForeground
        (white in both) can sit on it. Measured: white on Accent is 2.11:1, well under the 4.5:1
        needed for body text, in both themes.

        Use this wherever an accent-filled surface carries a caption. Roughly 9:1 on Accent and
        Accent2. If a surface can stop being accent-filled instead, prefer that: a themed surface
        with themed ink reaches 21:1 (see CoordinatePanelView).-->
    <SolidColorBrush x:Key="IRI.Maptor.Brushes.OnAccent.Text" Color="#FF1A1A1A"/>

</ResourceDictionary>
